    "q-104534": {
      "dom_id": "step-q104534",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "$(-3.2)^{2}=$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to calculate the product of $-3.2$ with itself:\n\n$$\n(-3.2)^{2}=(-3.2)\\cdot (-3.2)=(3.2)\\cdot (3.2)\n$$\n\nFirst, we ignore the decimal points and multiply as if both numbers were whole numbers:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,9\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,4\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $32\\times 32=1\\,024.$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in the first factor ($3.2$) and $1$ decimal place in the second factor ($3.2$), so their product will have $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n\nWe take our value of $1\\,024$ and insert a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places:\n\n$$\n10\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{24}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${3.2}^{2}=10.24.$",
